-</div></header><script src="/assets/vap-navigation-20261115.js" defer></script><main id="main"><div class="wrap"><p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Announcements archive</p><div class="news-archive vap-news"><div class="archive-hero"><span class="archive-eyebrow">VAP · NEWS ARCHIVE</span><h1>Announcements archive</h1><p>VAP research and website update history.</p></div><aside class="news-status"><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI and saved-evidence checks are distinct from independent fresh execution.</p></aside><p class="archive-history-label">Dates below are original publication dates. Later updates are identified when recorded. Historical notices describe the status at that time; their claims are not new confirmations of adoption, conformance or certification.</p><form class="archive-controls" hidden><label>Month<select name="month"><option value="">All</option><option value="2026-11">2026-11</option><option value="2026-10">2026-10</option></select></label><label class="archive-search">Search announcements<input type="search" name="search" autocomplete="off"></label><input type="hidden" name="category" value=""><button type="reset">Reset filters</button></form><p class="archive-count" id="archive-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-template="{shown} of {total} records">22 of 22 records</p><p class="archive-empty" id="archive-empty" hidden>No announcements match these filters.</p><section class="archive-month" id="month-2026-11"><h2>2026-11</h2><ul class="news-list"><li class="news-row" id="scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-25">2026-11-25</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-25-scitt-activity-incidents-android/">VSO records SCITT/VCP -07, IETF activity, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1</a></h3><p class="news-summary">SCITT/VCP -07, 40 list messages, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1 rollout. Drafts unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125" class="status"><h2>VSO records SCITT/VCP -07, IETF activity, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1</h2><p>SCITT/VCP -07, 40 list messages, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1 rollout. Drafts unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><ul><li><strong>IETF references:</strong> SCITT/VCP -07 was posted on 24 November 2026. RATS behavioral-evidence -03 was posted on 21 November (UTC). These are individual Internet-Drafts, not IETF Working Group adoptions or approvals.</li><li><strong>Activity record:</strong> the <a href="https://veritaschain.org/standardization/ietf-activity/">IETF SCITT mailing-list record</a> lists 40 messages by Tokachi Kamimura, compiled on 24 November. Participation is distinct from adoption or endorsement.</li><li><strong>Incident library:</strong> <a href="https://veritaschain.org/incidents/library/">78 records</a> retain source reports and VSO analysis as separate material. CERT-In’s AI-related observations and its account of payment tampering are separate; the record does not establish that AI caused those payments.</li><li><strong>VeraSnap:</strong> <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vap/cpp/verasnap/">Android 1.6.1</a> is rolling out in stages. Video capture, C2PA export, QR scanning and screen classification are not included in this Android version. Availability and platform differences should be checked in the published app guidance.</li></ul><p>The source review recorded 11 successful website CI jobs at main d962f80d and 39 VCP specification tests at dfed70b. These are first-party CI results, not independent reproduction. This notice does not update fixed tags or ZIPs; their historical results and known limitations remain separate from later main.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposals remain unadopted. Independent third-party VAP reproduction has not been established. These records do not establish full conformance, certification or production safety.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-25-scitt-activity-incidents-android/">Read the dated update, source revisions and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="ietf-interop-source-review-20261120" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-ietf-interop-source-review/">VSO updates VAP IETF references, interoperability guidance and the Commission incident record</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP Internet-Draft -03 references, IETF 127 research notes and external implementation guidance, and the European Commission source review. These updates do not establish adoption…</p><details class="archive-record" id="ietf-interop-source-review-20261120-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-ietf-interop-source-review-20261120" class="status"><h2>VSO updates VAP IETF references, interoperability guidance and the Commission incident record</h2><p>VAP Internet-Draft -03 references, IETF 127 research notes and external implementation guidance, and the European Commission source review. These updates do not establish adoption or independent reproduction.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain unadopted; independent third-party VAP reproduction has not been established. The individual VAP Internet-Draft has not been adopted by an IETF Working Group and has no IETF standing. The VSO specification remains v1.2.0 Draft 3.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-ietf-interop-source-review/">Read the update and sources</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance/">VSO reports change-evidence research and verifier repairs — SDK main and fixed release remain separate</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP research and verifier repairs. SDK: 125 tests at release, 186 on main; fixes absent from v0.1.0. MQL5 unfinished. Unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120" class="status"><h2>VSO reports change-evidence research and verifier repairs — SDK main and fixed release remain separate</h2><p>VAP research and verifier repairs. SDK: 125 tests at release, 186 on main; fixes absent from v0.1.0. MQL5 unfinished. Unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposals remain unadopted. Independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI, internal tests and inspection of public records are not independent fresh execution, full conformance, certification or proof of production safety.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance/">Read the four updates, revisions and unfinished work</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-18">2026-11-18</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-18-verasnap-verify-sdk-0-1-0/">VeraSnap Verify SDK 0.1.0: open-source server-side checks for CPP capture proofs</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VeritasChain Co., Ltd. published a Python verifier and device-key enrollment checks for VeraSnap proofs under Apache-2.0, for insurers that receive claim photos. It is a…</p><details class="archive-record" id="verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118" class="status"><h2>VeraSnap Verify SDK 0.1.0: open-source server-side checks for CPP capture proofs</h2><p>VeritasChain Co., Ltd. published a Python verifier and device-key enrollment checks for VeraSnap proofs under Apache-2.0, for insurers that receive claim photos. It is a first-party alpha release and has not been independently audited.</p><p>First-party alpha release by the operator of VSO; not independently audited, not a conformance test suite and not a certification. A proof shows when and on which device a capture was recorded; it does not show that the picture is true.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-18-verasnap-verify-sdk-0-1-0/">Read the release notice, checks and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="verification-hardening-20261115" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-15">2026-11-15</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and…</p><details class="archive-record" id="verification-hardening-20261115-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verification-hardening-20261115" class="status"><h2>VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</h2><p>Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and first-party CI remain distinct.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI, separate-language recomputation, saved-evidence rechecks and an independent fresh run are distinct. Merges and synthetic successes do not establish full conformance, production safety or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">Read changes, revisions and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate.…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" class="status"><h2>Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</h2><p>Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. First-party CI is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article demonstrates no VAP/VCP prevention capability, full conformance or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Read the source distinctions and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="snowball-grok-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</a></h3><p class="news-summary">A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="snowball-grok-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-snowball-grok-20261114" class="status"><h2>Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</h2><p>A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI success is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article establishes no VAP/VCP prevention record, full conformance or certification for these cases.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Read corrections, estimates and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="registry-release-20261113" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-13">2026-11-13</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten source reviews added; the fixed demo now has a known-issue notice. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="registry-release-20261113-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-registry-release-20261113" class="status"><h2>VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</h2><p>Website PR #224 adds ten reviews, bringing the registry to 64 entries: 19 registered and 45 source-verified, pending registration. The ten additions belong to the latter category. They are not ten newly confirmed incidents, and the total does not mean 64 registered cases.</p><p>PR #68 merged the explicit input policy into main. It is absent from the fixed tag, fixed ZIP and original 32-test record. This update changes the public explanation only: the tag, all five assets, checksums and historical execution evidence are retained. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Reports must pin the implementation commit.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. Source checks, synthetic observations and CI described here are first-party work. Merging or passing CI does not establish full normative conformance, adoption, certification or production suitability.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">Read updates, pinned revisions and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/releases/tag/vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0">GitHub release</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="signature-source-20261112" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-12">2026-11-12</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</a></h3><p class="news-summary">13 Nov: site CI at 720852c passed 110 image comparisons. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="signature-source-20261112-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-signature-source-20261112" class="status"><h2>VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</h2><p>VAP PR #68 strengthens Ed25519 input rejection in the experimental Python/Node interop demo. The fix is merged into main (35e56ba; included in e00ee5a). It is NOT included in the fixed vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0 ZIP, which remains at cbd4502. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">Read source revisions, the main/ZIP distinction and limitations</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261113"><h3>13 November follow-up: 110 image comparisons passed in site main CI</h3><p>Website vcp-site fix merge <code>720852c</code> completed all six workflows and 13 jobs. All 110 image comparisons passed with zero failures and zero raster-noise allowances. Incorrect-CSS rejection and animation checks also passed; comparison criteria were not relaxed. These are first-party CI results for this fixed website revision.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. This is not a new research-implementation test or independent reproduction. Earlier failures, historical test records and the distinction between fixed distributions and main are retained.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/#main-ci-20261113">Read the first-party CI revision, results and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-site/actions/runs/43330507404">CI · 720852c</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cloud-evidence-20261108" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-08">2026-11-08</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation and maintenance. The demo was unpublished at the initial review; a later experimental prerelease is…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cloud-evidence-20261108-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cloud-evidence-20261108" class="status"><h2>VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</h2><p>Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation, Explorer dependency maintenance, local-settings guards and incident-source records. PR #61 is release preparation and was unpublished at the initial review. A later experimental prerelease at 12:09 JST on 8 November is recorded separately in the linked article. The research is unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Test and CI records are first-party checks, not independent confirmation.</p><p>All cloud experiments are synthetic and operated by the same party; no live cloud calls were made. They do not prove Azure origin, complete observation, independent custody, latestness, third-party timestamps, power-loss durability or production readiness. A valid older snapshot can remain valid without a separately retained contradictory checkpoint. Verification of custody does not grant permission to publish evidence. First-party CI is not independent reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">Read the ten updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="payment-research-20261107" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-07">2026-11-07</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP #52–#58 cover payment evidence, dispatch recovery, two-person approval and collection, plus school-AI and consumer-agent design notes. First-party CI only; unadopted,…</p><details class="archive-record" id="payment-research-20261107-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-payment-research-20261107" class="status"><h2>VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</h2><p>VAP #52–#58 were merged on 6 November. First-party payment-research CI checked 57 offline-evidence, 28 dispatch/recovery, 20 authorization and 25 collector tests separately. School-AI and consumer-agent updates are documents; the latter’s eight review cases are unexecuted. Extensions and proposals remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>All experiments use first-party synthetic environments. A holder of raw mock-provider credentials can bypass the wrapper. Complete route coverage, independent custody, external anchoring, OS privilege separation and full proposal conformance are not established. A signed ACK does not prove truth, completeness or continuing retention.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">Read the seven updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="research-sdk-20261105" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-05">2026-11-05</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</a></h3><p class="news-summary">5 Nov: a18cda8 site CI completed (110 image comparisons; 55 regression tests). Research remains unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="research-sdk-20261105-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-research-sdk-20261105" class="status"><h2>VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</h2><p>Merged research separates control observations, wallet authorization and execution evidence. SDK fixes and reproduction notes are available; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. The results below are first-party CI and internal research checks, not an independent assessment, certification, production-readiness determination or proof of complete observation.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">Read the update and source records</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261105"><h3>5 November follow-up: site main CI completed</h3><p>Website main <code>a18cda8</code> completed all five workflows and 12 jobs, including 110 image comparisons, 55 regression tests and a 428-page CSP crawl. Chinese VeraSnap image pairs matched exactly at desktop and mobile widths. Comparison criteria were not relaxed.</p><p>This is first-party website CI, not an independent reproduction result. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Historical test records remain attached to their original revisions.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/#main-ci-20261105">Read the main CI completion results and scope</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-corrections-20261103" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-03">2026-11-03</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP source/hash, public Explorer and 23 merged corrections. First-party checks are distinct from independent reproduction; experimental extensions remain unadopted.</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-corrections-20261103-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-corrections-20261103" class="status"><h2>VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</h2><p>23 merged repository corrections: current VAP text and digest, bounded Explorer hash-chain checks, authentication fixes and historical-status disclosures. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>These are disclosure corrections, bounded implementation repairs and first-party checks. They do not establish full VCP/VAP conformance, certification, production readiness or independent third-party reproduction. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. A local test reported in a PR, first-party CI, this website deployment check and an independent new execution are different records.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">Read the corrections and their limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261102" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2026-11-02</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #30–#34 add synthetic permission and receiver-state experiments. Latest first-party CI passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS job. Extensions remain unadopted; independent…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261102-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
+</div></header><script src="/assets/vap-navigation-20261115.js" defer></script><main id="main"><div class="wrap"><p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Announcements archive</p><div class="news-archive vap-news"><div class="archive-hero"><span class="archive-eyebrow">VAP · NEWS ARCHIVE</span><h1>Announcements archive</h1><p>VAP research and website update history.</p></div><aside class="news-status"><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI and saved-evidence checks are distinct from independent fresh execution.</p></aside><p class="archive-history-label">Dates below are original publication dates. Later updates are identified when recorded. Historical notices describe the status at that time; their claims are not new confirmations of adoption, conformance or certification.</p><form class="archive-controls" hidden><label>Month<select name="month"><option value="">All</option><option value="2026-11">2026-11</option><option value="2026-10">2026-10</option></select></label><label class="archive-search">Search announcements<input type="search" name="search" autocomplete="off"></label><input type="hidden" name="category" value=""><button type="reset">Reset filters</button></form><p class="archive-count" id="archive-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-template="{shown} of {total} records">23 of 23 records</p><p class="archive-empty" id="archive-empty" hidden>No announcements match these filters.</p><section class="archive-month" id="month-2026-11"><h2>2026-11</h2><ul class="news-list"><li class="news-row" id="sdk-seal-explorer-incident-20261127" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-27">2026-11-27</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-27-sdk-seal-explorer-incident-update/">VSO records SDK seal recovery, Explorer source updates and 85 incident records</a></h3><p class="news-summary">SDK and Explorer source updates; 40 VCP CLI tests; 85 incident records. Extensions unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="sdk-seal-explorer-incident-20261127-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-sdk-seal-explorer-incident-20261127" class="status"><h2>VSO records SDK seal recovery, Explorer source updates and 85 incident records</h2><p>SDK and Explorer source updates; 40 VCP CLI tests; 85 incident records. Extensions unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><ul><li><strong>VCP SDK:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-sdk/pull/25">PR #25</a> checks that every input event has the same Header.PolicyID before signing and stages the event and AnchorRecord output pair, with recovery if the second replacement fails. The two replacements are not one atomic transaction; crashes or failed rollback still require inspecting recovery files. Main is cb6a69e; the documented installation pin is 28d46e8. No new fixed release was published.</li><li><strong>Explorer source:</strong> the API adds the documented /v1/health endpoint while retaining /health; API dependencies and GUI build tools were updated. Source CI success does not by itself establish deployment of the public GUI bundle or the separately hosted API runtime. A health response is not evidence verification.</li><li><strong>VCP event-validation CLI:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-spec/pull/46">PR #46</a> treats unresolved schema references as configuration errors and prevents partial batch results on stdout. <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-spec/actions/runs/45918910642">40 tests passed in first-party CI at 81513e5</a>; this is not additional cryptographic verification or independent reproduction. Normative text, schemas and fixed releases are unchanged.</li><li><strong>Incident library:</strong> <a href="https://veritaschain.org/incidents/library/">the library now contains 85 records, up from 78</a>, with follow-ups to two existing records kept separate from new entries. Source reports, related-party statements, reporting and VSO analysis remain distinct; record counts do not establish confirmed AI causation.</li></ul><p>Experimental extensions and proposals remain unadopted; independent third-party VAP reproduction has not been established. Fixed tags and ZIPs, prior test records and the VAP specification references and hashes are unchanged. See the dated article for exact source revisions, deployment boundaries and limitations.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-27-sdk-seal-explorer-incident-update/">Read the source updates, CI scope and fixed-release boundaries</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-25">2026-11-25</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-25-scitt-activity-incidents-android/">VSO records SCITT/VCP -07, IETF activity, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1</a></h3><p class="news-summary">SCITT/VCP -07, 40 list messages, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1 rollout. Drafts unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-scitt-activity-incidents-android-20261125" class="status"><h2>VSO records SCITT/VCP -07, IETF activity, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1</h2><p>SCITT/VCP -07, 40 list messages, 78 incident records and Android 1.6.1 rollout. Drafts unadopted; independent VAP reproduction not established.</p><ul><li><strong>IETF references:</strong> SCITT/VCP -07 was posted on 24 November 2026. RATS behavioral-evidence -03 was posted on 21 November (UTC). These are individual Internet-Drafts, not IETF Working Group adoptions or approvals.</li><li><strong>Activity record:</strong> the <a href="https://veritaschain.org/standardization/ietf-activity/">IETF SCITT mailing-list record</a> lists 40 messages by Tokachi Kamimura, compiled on 24 November. Participation is distinct from adoption or endorsement.</li><li><strong>Incident library:</strong> <a href="https://veritaschain.org/incidents/library/">78 records</a> retain source reports and VSO analysis as separate material. CERT-In’s AI-related observations and its account of payment tampering are separate; the record does not establish that AI caused those payments.</li><li><strong>VeraSnap:</strong> <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vap/cpp/verasnap/">Android 1.6.1</a> is rolling out in stages. Video capture, C2PA export, QR scanning and screen classification are not included in this Android version. Availability and platform differences should be checked in the published app guidance.</li></ul><p>The source review recorded 11 successful website CI jobs at main d962f80d and 39 VCP specification tests at dfed70b. These are first-party CI results, not independent reproduction. This notice does not update fixed tags or ZIPs; their historical results and known limitations remain separate from later main.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposals remain unadopted. Independent third-party VAP reproduction has not been established. These records do not establish full conformance, certification or production safety.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-25-scitt-activity-incidents-android/">Read the dated update, source revisions and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="ietf-interop-source-review-20261120" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-ietf-interop-source-review/">VSO updates VAP IETF references, interoperability guidance and the Commission incident record</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP Internet-Draft -03 references, IETF 127 research notes and external implementation guidance, and the European Commission source review. These updates do not establish adoption…</p><details class="archive-record" id="ietf-interop-source-review-20261120-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-ietf-interop-source-review-20261120" class="status"><h2>VSO updates VAP IETF references, interoperability guidance and the Commission incident record</h2><p>VAP Internet-Draft -03 references, IETF 127 research notes and external implementation guidance, and the European Commission source review. These updates do not establish adoption or independent reproduction.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain unadopted; independent third-party VAP reproduction has not been established. The individual VAP Internet-Draft has not been adopted by an IETF Working Group and has no IETF standing. The VSO specification remains v1.2.0 Draft 3.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-ietf-interop-source-review/">Read the update and sources</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-20">2026-11-20</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance/">VSO reports change-evidence research and verifier repairs — SDK main and fixed release remain separate</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP research and verifier repairs. SDK: 125 tests at release, 186 on main; fixes absent from v0.1.0. MQL5 unfinished. Unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance-20261120" class="status"><h2>VSO reports change-evidence research and verifier repairs — SDK main and fixed release remain separate</h2><p>VAP research and verifier repairs. SDK: 125 tests at release, 186 on main; fixes absent from v0.1.0. MQL5 unfinished. Unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposals remain unadopted. Independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI, internal tests and inspection of public records are not independent fresh execution, full conformance, certification or proof of production safety.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-20-change-evidence-verifier-maintenance/">Read the four updates, revisions and unfinished work</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-18">2026-11-18</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-18-verasnap-verify-sdk-0-1-0/">VeraSnap Verify SDK 0.1.0: open-source server-side checks for CPP capture proofs</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VeritasChain Co., Ltd. published a Python verifier and device-key enrollment checks for VeraSnap proofs under Apache-2.0, for insurers that receive claim photos. It is a…</p><details class="archive-record" id="verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verasnap-verify-sdk-20261118" class="status"><h2>VeraSnap Verify SDK 0.1.0: open-source server-side checks for CPP capture proofs</h2><p>VeritasChain Co., Ltd. published a Python verifier and device-key enrollment checks for VeraSnap proofs under Apache-2.0, for insurers that receive claim photos. It is a first-party alpha release and has not been independently audited.</p><p>First-party alpha release by the operator of VSO; not independently audited, not a conformance test suite and not a certification. A proof shows when and on which device a capture was recorded; it does not show that the picture is true.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-18-verasnap-verify-sdk-0-1-0/">Read the release notice, checks and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="verification-hardening-20261115" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-15">2026-11-15</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and…</p><details class="archive-record" id="verification-hardening-20261115-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-verification-hardening-20261115" class="status"><h2>VSO reports 23 verification, SDK and Explorer improvements</h2><p>Five areas cover configured-key validation, safer inputs and outputs, unresolved verdicts, evidence-review research and the public Explorer. Current main, fixed distributions and first-party CI remain distinct.</p><p>Experimental extensions and proposed repairs remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI, separate-language recomputation, saved-evidence rechecks and an independent fresh run are distinct. Merges and synthetic successes do not establish full conformance, production safety or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-15-verification-hardening-explorer-update/">Read changes, revisions and limits</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate.…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cursor-apify-epoch-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cursor-apify-epoch-20261114" class="status"><h2>Cursor follow-up, Apify and Epoch AI: secrets, permissions and evaluation boundaries</h2><p>Reviewing three 13 November reports and updates, with Cursor identified as a follow-up. Official reports, participant accounts, press reporting and VSO analysis are separate. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. First-party CI is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article demonstrates no VAP/VCP prevention capability, full conformance or certification.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-cursor-apify-epoch-source-review/">Read the source distinctions and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="snowball-grok-20261114" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-14">2026-11-14</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</a></h3><p class="news-summary">A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="snowball-grok-20261114-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-snowball-grok-20261114" class="status"><h2>Snowball and Grok Build reports: AI actions, publication permissions and evidence limits</h2><p>A source review of Snowball and Grok Build separates the Cisco correction, researcher estimates and VSO analysis. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. First-party CI success is distinct from independent fresh execution. This article establishes no VAP/VCP prevention record, full conformance or certification for these cases.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-14-snowball-grok-source-review/">Read corrections, estimates and VSO analysis</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="registry-release-20261113" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-13">2026-11-13</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten source reviews added; the fixed demo now has a known-issue notice. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not…</p><details class="archive-record" id="registry-release-20261113-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-registry-release-20261113" class="status"><h2>VSO adds ten source reviews and a fixed-demo known-issue notice</h2><p>Website PR #224 adds ten reviews, bringing the registry to 64 entries: 19 registered and 45 source-verified, pending registration. The ten additions belong to the latter category. They are not ten newly confirmed incidents, and the total does not mean 64 registered cases.</p><p>PR #68 merged the explicit input policy into main. It is absent from the fixed tag, fixed ZIP and original 32-test record. This update changes the public explanation only: the tag, all five assets, checksums and historical execution evidence are retained. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Reports must pin the implementation commit.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. Source checks, synthetic observations and CI described here are first-party work. Merging or passing CI does not establish full normative conformance, adoption, certification or production suitability.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-13-registry-release-known-issue/">Read updates, pinned revisions and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vap-spec/releases/tag/vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0">GitHub release</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="signature-source-20261112" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-12">2026-11-12</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</a></h3><p class="news-summary">13 Nov: site CI at 720852c passed 110 image comparisons. Signature fix: main only, absent from fixed ZIP. Extensions unadopted; independent reproduction not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="signature-source-20261112-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-signature-source-20261112" class="status"><h2>VSO updates VAP references and research status; signature fix is on main only</h2><p>VAP PR #68 strengthens Ed25519 input rejection in the experimental Python/Node interop demo. The fix is merged into main (35e56ba; included in e00ee5a). It is NOT included in the fixed vap-interop-demo-v0.2.0 ZIP, which remains at cbd4502. No replacement ZIP or new release is announced. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/">Read source revisions, the main/ZIP distinction and limitations</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261113"><h3>13 November follow-up: 110 image comparisons passed in site main CI</h3><p>Website vcp-site fix merge <code>720852c</code> completed all six workflows and 13 jobs. All 110 image comparisons passed with zero failures and zero raster-noise allowances. Incorrect-CSS rejection and animation checks also passed; comparison criteria were not relaxed. These are first-party CI results for this fixed website revision.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. This is not a new research-implementation test or independent reproduction. Earlier failures, historical test records and the distinction between fixed distributions and main are retained.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-12-vap-signature-source-update/#main-ci-20261113">Read the first-party CI revision, results and limits</a> · <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-site/actions/runs/43330507404">CI · 720852c</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="cloud-evidence-20261108" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-08">2026-11-08</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation and maintenance. The demo was unpublished at the initial review; a later experimental prerelease is…</p><details class="archive-record" id="cloud-evidence-20261108-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-cloud-evidence-20261108" class="status"><h2>VSO reports ten merged cloud-evidence and maintenance updates</h2><p>Ten merged PRs cover cloud-evidence research, interop release preparation, Explorer dependency maintenance, local-settings guards and incident-source records. PR #61 is release preparation and was unpublished at the initial review. A later experimental prerelease at 12:09 JST on 8 November is recorded separately in the linked article. The research is unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Test and CI records are first-party checks, not independent confirmation.</p><p>All cloud experiments are synthetic and operated by the same party; no live cloud calls were made. They do not prove Azure origin, complete observation, independent custody, latestness, third-party timestamps, power-loss durability or production readiness. A valid older snapshot can remain valid without a separately retained contradictory checkpoint. Verification of custody does not grant permission to publish evidence. First-party CI is not independent reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-08-cloud-evidence-maintenance-update/">Read the ten updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="payment-research-20261107" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-07">2026-11-07</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP #52–#58 cover payment evidence, dispatch recovery, two-person approval and collection, plus school-AI and consumer-agent design notes. First-party CI only; unadopted,…</p><details class="archive-record" id="payment-research-20261107-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-payment-research-20261107" class="status"><h2>VSO publishes seven VAP payment-evidence research and AI design updates</h2><p>VAP #52–#58 were merged on 6 November. First-party payment-research CI checked 57 offline-evidence, 28 dispatch/recovery, 20 authorization and 25 collector tests separately. School-AI and consumer-agent updates are documents; the latter’s eight review cases are unexecuted. Extensions and proposals remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>All experiments use first-party synthetic environments. A holder of raw mock-provider credentials can bypass the wrapper. Complete route coverage, independent custody, external anchoring, OS privilege separation and full proposal conformance are not established. A signed ACK does not prove truth, completeness or continuing retention.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-07-payment-evidence-research-update/">Read the seven updates, CI and limitations</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="research-sdk-20261105" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-05">2026-11-05</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</a></h3><p class="news-summary">5 Nov: a18cda8 site CI completed (110 image comparisons; 55 regression tests). Research remains unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><details class="archive-record" id="research-sdk-20261105-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-research-sdk-20261105" class="status"><h2>VAP research, SDK updates and external reproduction notes</h2><p>Merged research separates control observations, wallet authorization and execution evidence. SDK fixes and reproduction notes are available; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction has not been established. The results below are first-party CI and internal research checks, not an independent assessment, certification, production-readiness determination or proof of complete observation.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/">Read the update and source records</a></p><div id="original-main-ci-20261105"><h3>5 November follow-up: site main CI completed</h3><p>Website main <code>a18cda8</code> completed all five workflows and 12 jobs, including 110 image comparisons, 55 regression tests and a 428-page CSP crawl. Chinese VeraSnap image pairs matched exactly at desktop and mobile widths. Comparison criteria were not relaxed.</p><p>This is first-party website CI, not an independent reproduction result. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established. Historical test records remain attached to their original revisions.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-05-vap-research-sdk-reproduction/#main-ci-20261105">Read the main CI completion results and scope</a></p></div></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-corrections-20261103" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-03">2026-11-03</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</a></h3><p class="news-summary">VAP source/hash, public Explorer and 23 merged corrections. First-party checks are distinct from independent reproduction; experimental extensions remain unadopted.</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-corrections-20261103-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-corrections-20261103" class="status"><h2>VSO updates verification-status disclosures and the public Explorer</h2><p>23 merged repository corrections: current VAP text and digest, bounded Explorer hash-chain checks, authentication fixes and historical-status disclosures. Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>These are disclosure corrections, bounded implementation repairs and first-party checks. They do not establish full VCP/VAP conformance, certification, production readiness or independent third-party reproduction. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. A local test reported in a PR, first-party CI, this website deployment check and an independent new execution are different records.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-03-verification-status-explorer-corrections/">Read the corrections and their limits →</a></p></section></div></details></div></li><li class="news-row" id="github-update-20261102" data-news-record data-month="2026-11" data-category="research"><div class="news-meta"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2026-11-02</time></div><div><h3><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</a></h3><p class="news-summary">Evidect #30–#34 add synthetic permission and receiver-state experiments. Latest first-party CI passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS job. Extensions remain unadopted; independent…</p><details class="archive-record" id="github-update-20261102-record"><summary>Read the archived notice</summary><p class="archive-history-label">Historical notice, including existing corrections</p><div class="archive-original"><section id="original-github-update-20261102" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">2 November: five service-permission and receiver-history research updates</h2><p>Evidect #30–#34 add service-permission rechecks, saved ten-case verification, checkpoint expiry/generations/key revocation and challenge-bound checks against a separate store. Latest merged eeeacf7 passed 306 tests per Ubuntu/macOS first-party CI job (44 new + 262 existing).</p><p>These are same-controller synthetic experiments. Separate processes and keys do not establish independent administration; both-store rollback and other limits remain. Extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. The 137-test record, earlier results and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-11-02-service-permission-receiver-state/">Read the five updates and their limits →</a></p></section>
